'''Tera Sinube''' was a [[Cosian]] [[Gender|male]] [[Jedi Master]] who lived during the height and later descent of the [[Galactic Republic]]. Sinube was the [[marshal]] of a [[Jedi outpost]] on [[Derra IV|Derra]] during the [[High Republic Era]], and sat on the [[Jedi High Council]] sometime before the [[Invasion of Naboo]]. In [[21 BBY]], [[Jedi]] [[Padawan]] [[Ahsoka Tano]] enlisted his help tracking down her stolen [[lightsaber]] and by [[9 BBY]], Sinube had been [[Death|killed]] and was entombed at [[Fortress Inquisitorius]] on the [[moon]] [[Nur]].

==Biography==
===High Republic Era and Pre-Naboo Crisis===
{{Quote|That is Tera Sinube. He's an elder Jedi. He happens to be an expert on the Coruscant crime world.|Jocasta Nu|audio=ThatIsTeraSinube-LL.flac|<ref name="Lightsaber Lost" />}}
Tera Sinube was [[Reproduction|born]] before [[428 BBY]].<ref name="Birth" /> In [[231 BBY]],<ref name="Rising Storm date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of ''[[The High Republic: The Rising Storm]]'' to [[231 BBY]].</ref> Sinube had recently risen to the rank of [[Jedi Master]], and was [[marshal]] of a [[Derra Outpost|Jedi outpost]] on [[Derra IV|Derra]]. When the nearby [[planet]] [[Cyclor]] was [[First Battle of Cyclor|attacked]] by the [[Nihil]] [[pirate]]s, Master [[Stellan Gios]] contacted Sinube for assistance, and he dispatched the legendary [[Ikkrukkian]] Master [[Porter Engle]] to lead a [[drift]] of [[Jedi Vector]]s to assist.<ref name="Rising Storm">''[[The High Republic: The Rising Storm]]''</ref>

As a [[Jedi investigator]], Sinube was an expert in the [[planet]] [[Coruscant]]'s criminal [[Coruscant Underworld|underworld]]. His connection to [[the Force]] allowed him to solve crimes faster than seasoned [[detective]]s in the [[Coruscant Security Force|Coruscant Police]].<ref name="Databank">{{Databank|tera-sinube|Tera Sinube}}</ref> Decades before the Invasion of [[Naboo]], Sinube was the leader of the [[Jedi Initiate|Jedi youngling]] [[Hawk-Bat Clan]], whose members included [[Zang Arraira]], [[Arath Tarrex]], [[Sifo-Dyas]], and [[Dooku]]. While Dooku was still a [[Jedi Initiate|Jedi youngling]], Master Sinube traveled to [[Serenno]] along with Dooku, [[Sifo-Dyas]], [[Grand Master]] [[Yoda]], Master [[Yula Braylon]], and many other younglings and masters for the galactic festival there. He and Master Braylon rushed to Yoda's aid when the youngling Sifo-Dyas accidentally knocked into him. He selected Zang to be his Padawan apprentice in [[86 BBY]], and had a seat on the Jedi High Council by the [[85 BBY|next year]].<ref name="Dooku: Jedi Lost" />

While seated on the Jedi High Council, Sinube attended the funeral for Master [[Katri]], who had died on [[Raxus Secundus]].<ref name="Resolve">{{TOTJ|Resolve (episode)}}</ref> Some time following that, he was also present when the [[Padawan]] [[Cere Junda]] met with the Council in the fallout of the [[Battle for Ontotho|battle]] for [[Ontotho]] and was [[Knighting Ceremony|granted]] the rank of [[Jedi Knight]] for her conduct.<ref name="Dark Temple 5">[[Jedi Fallen Order - Dark Temple 5|''Jedi Fallen Order - Dark Temple'' 5]]</ref> Sinube would leave his position on the council sometime before the [[Invasion of Naboo]]<ref name="TPM">{{Film|I}}</ref> in [[32 BBY]].<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref>

===Adventure with Ahsoka Tano===
{{Quote|You ran off in such a hurry. I trust you didn't mean to be rude.''"<br />"''I have nothing more to say to you, Jedi.''"<br />"''Well, perhaps you meant to be a ''little'' rude.|Tera Sinube and Ione Marcy|<ref name="Lightsaber Lost">{{TCW|Lightsaber Lost}}</ref>}}
[[File:SinubeNuTano-LL.png|thumb|left|300px|Sinube meets Ahsoka Tano, the Padawan learner to Anakin Skywalker.]]
During the [[Clone Wars]], Sinube had fallen asleep in the middle of some research in the Archives when he was approached by [[Padawan]] [[Ahsoka Tano]] for help in recovering her [[lightsaber]], which had been stolen by a thief named [[Bannamu]]. Sinube elected to accompany the girl, not having been on an assignment in many years and confident that she would not succeed unless she learned to be patient and take things slowly. Tracking Bannamu to the [[Spider Arms Hostel]], Sinube used a mind trick on the attendant to get past before the two Jedi located and confronted the thief in his room. Sinube was forced to interject on Bannamu's behalf to keep Tano from causing the [[Patrolian]] bodily harm in her anger; under duress, Bannamu revealed that he had sold the lightsaber to [[Nack Movers]], a well-known criminal and assassin in the Coruscant underworld. When they traveled to Movers' apartment building, Sinube saw that the lock was broken and surmised it to be the Trandoshan's residence. Inside, they found the corpse of Movers and a terrified girl who identified herself as [[Ione Marcy]] and who claimed that a group of men had killed Movers.<ref name="Lightsaber Lost" />

Tano searched the other rooms whilst Sinube remained behind with Ione, suspecting her of knowing more than she was letting on about what happened to Movers. Tano shortly reported being attacked by an intruder who had her lightsaber, a female [[Terrelian Jango Jumper]], which contradicted Marcy's earlier claims. Sinube summoned the authorities and discretely planted a tracker on Marcy's back, then proceeded to interrogate her further on what had happend. Marcy's evasive and contradictory statements convinced the elderly Jedi that she was involved in Movers' [[death]] and ordered the arriving police droids to arrest her, only for Marcy to escape. Undaunted, Sinube borrowed a speeder bike from the police and picked up Tano before following the tracker signal to a nearby train station where they found Marcy and her accomplice, [[Cassilyda Cryar|Cassie Cryar]].<ref name="Lightsaber Lost" />

[[File:SinubeVsCryar-LL.png|thumb|right|300px|Sinube defeated Cryar in a matter of seconds.]]
Whilst police droids apprehended Marcy, Tano chased Cryar to the next station where the criminal used the stolen lightsaber to take two hostages in order to deter further Jedi pursuit. When the train door opened, however, she found Sinube waiting for her. Drawing his lightsaber from within his cane, Sinube engaged Cryar in a very brief duel before disarming and knocking her unconscious with a single move. Tano and Sinube then returned to the Jedi Temple, where Sinube asked Tano to pass on what she had learned from the situation. Visiting a class of younglings being taught by Master Yoda, whom Sinube greeted as an old friend, he then watched as Tano informed the younglings of the importance of keeping their lightsaber with them at all times.<ref name="Lightsaber Lost" />

===Later war and death===
{{Quote|This isn't just a fortress. It's a tomb.|Obi-Wan Kenobi, upon seeing Tera Sinube's preserved corpse|<ref name="Kenobi IV">{{Kenobi|Part IV}}</ref>}}
Following their adventure, Sinube continued to take interest in and observe Tano's Jedi training, at one point supervising a test in which Tano practiced against [[Battle droid remote|new training remotes]] that were designed to simulate [[battle droid]]s in the [[Jedi Temple dojo]].<ref name="Practice Makes Perfect">{{TOTJ|Practice Makes Perfect (episode)}}</ref> In [[20 BBY]],<ref name="Date">{{TCWcanondates|510}}</ref> Sinube volunteered his [[astromech droid]], [[M5-BZ]], for a [[Mission to steal a Separatist encryption module|mission]] to infiltrate a [[Aut-O's flagship|Separatist dreadnought]] and steal an [[encryption module]] that was scrambling communications within the region.<ref name="Secret Weapons">{{TCW|Secret Weapons}}</ref> He also trained [[Jedi Initiate|younglings]] in the [[Jedi training|Jedi arts]] at the [[Imperial Palace|temple]] on Coruscant, where they were present to see the fallen Padawan [[Barriss Offee]] [[Duel at the Jedi Temple|duel]] Tano's master, [[Anakin Skywalker]], who defeated Offee before Sinube and the younglings. Sinube had drawn his saber ready to protect the younglings if needed but it was not.<ref name="The Wrong Jedi">{{TCW|The Wrong Jedi}}</ref>

[[File:Tera_Sinube_Corpse.png|thumb|left|260px|Obi-Wan Kenobi discovered Sinube's preserved corpse at Fortress Inquisitorius.]]
By [[9 BBY]], Sinube had been killed<ref name="Death" /> and was entombed at [[Fortress Inquisitorius]], the headquarters of the [[Inquisitorius]], on the [[water]] [[moon]] [[Nur]]. His petrified corpse was one of the first in display, being located at the left hand side of one of the [[Jedi tomb|tomb's]] entrances. Whilst infiltrating the base to [[Rescue of Princess Leia (9 BBY)|rescue]] [[Princess]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]], Kenobi found himself in the tomb, where he was horrified to discover the corpses of Sinube and many other dead Jedi. After informing former [[Imperial officer]] [[Tala Durith]] about the tomb, Kenobi ran from it to continue his mission.<ref name="Kenobi IV">{{Kenobi|Part IV}}</ref>

==Powers and abilities==
Tera Sinube was an old and experienced Jedi Master. He was a skilled and resourceful investigator and, despite his age, he remained a skilled lightsaber duelist.<ref name="Lightsaber Lost" />
Aside from his abilities as a Jedi Sinube was able to pilot [[Spiral-class Viz-Core Eviscerator|Eviscerator starships]]<ref name="High Republic Adventures 2023 15">[[The High Republic Adventures (2023) 15|''The High Republic Adventures'' (2023) 15]]</ref> and [[Vector V-3.2 Tandem|Jedi Vectors]].<ref name="High Republic Adventures 2023 18">[[The High Republic Adventures (2023) 18|''The High Republic Adventures'' (2023) 18]]</ref>

==Equipment==
[[File:TeraSinubesLightsaberIgnited-LightsaberLost.jpg|thumb|250px|Tera Sinube's light blue lightsaber cane]]
Sinube was the owner of [[M5-BZ]]<ref name="Secret Weapons" /> and wielded a [[Tera Sinube's lightsaber|lightsaber]] with a very light [[Color|blue]] blade that could also be used as a cane.<ref name="FB">{{Facebook|username=DaveFiloni|url=notes/dave-filoni/qa/10150219391017571|name=[[Dave Filoni]]|date=2011-03-23|archivedate=20160101103626|archivefile=File:DaveFiloniQA-Facebook.png}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
Tera Sinube first appeared in the ninth episode of the [[The Clone Wars: Season Two|second season]] of Star Wars: The Clone Wars, "[[Grievous Intrigue]]<ref name="Lightsaber Lost" />," which aired on [[January 1]], [[2010]], but was created for "[[Lightsaber Lost]]," the eleventh episode of the season, which was produced first and released on [[January 22]] of that same year.<ref name="Lightsaber Lost Trivia">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/lightsaber-lost-trivia-gallery|text="Lightsaber Lost" Trivia Gallery}} {{C|Slide 1}}</ref>  For "Lightsaber Lost", Sinube's only speaking role for the series, he was voiced by veteran voice actor [[Gregory Baldwin]].<ref name="Lightsaber Lost" />

Tera Sinube was adapted from unused concept art for an alien senator in [[Star Wars: Episode I The Phantom Menace|''Star Wars'': Episode I ''The Phantom Menace'']]<ref name="Lightsaber Lost Trivia" /> by [[Terryl Whitlatch]].<ref name="Insider Guide">{{[[Star Wars: Episode I Insider's Guide]]}}</ref> <ref name="Complete Saga">{{[[Star Wars: The Complete Saga]]]]}}</ref>

He made his first live-action appearance in the [[2022]] television series ''[[Star Wars: Obi-Wan Kenobi]]'', in which his corpse was revealed to be preserved in a tomb on Nur during the [[Part IV|fourth episode]], which was released on [[June 8]], 2022.<ref name="Kenobi IV" />

